        <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">Hotel Base</div>
            <div class="value">Nine Tree Premier Myeongdong 2</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #64748b;">4 Nights ~$900 total</div>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
            <div class="label">Priority Spa</div>
            <div class="value">Aquafield Spa Goyang</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #64748b;">Day 4 Relaxing Hot Springs</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Day 1 -->
<div class="day-card">
    <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 1</span>
        <span class="day-title">Arrival, Myeongdong Street Food &amp; Bib Gourmand</span>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">3:45 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Arrival &amp; Transit:</strong> Land at Incheon Airport (ICN T1). Board the non-stop AREX Express Train to Seoul Station (43 mins), then take a quick taxi to <strong>Nine Tree Premier Hotel Myeongdong 2</strong>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">6:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Hotel Check-in:</strong> Unpack, refresh, and settle into Myeongdong.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">7:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Myeongdong Night Market:</strong> Explore the pedestrian avenues. Sample street eats: <strong>Flame-Blowtorched Beef Skewers</strong>, warm <strong>Gyeran-ppang (Egg Bread)</strong>, <em>tteokbokki</em>, and sweet stuffed <em>hoteok</em>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">9:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Sit-Down Noodles &amp; Dumplings:</strong> Walk over to <strong>Myeongdong Kyoja</strong> (Michelin Bib Gourmand) for hand-cut noodle soup (<em>kalguksu</em>) and pork dumplings (<em>mandu</em>).</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Day 2 -->
<div class="day-card">
    <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 2</span>
        <span class="day-title">Inwangsan Hike, Palaces &amp; Hanok Village</span>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">8:30 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Grab artisanal coffee and pastries at <strong>Cafe Onion Anguk</strong> (restored hanok bakery).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">9:30 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Inwangsan Mountain Hike (Active Outdoor Trail):</strong> Hike along the historic wooden and stone paths of the Seoul City Wall to the 338m summit for 360-degree views of the cityscape.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">12:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Gyeongbokgung Palace:</strong> Descend near Changuimun Gate and explore the Joseon Dynasty's primary royal palace. Rent a <em>Hanbok</em> for free admission.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">1:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Lunch at Tosokchon Samgyetang:</strong> Refuel after the hike with traditional ginseng chicken soup.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">3:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Bukchon Hanok Village &amp; Insadong:</strong> Walk Bukchon's preserved residential alleys, then wander down Insadong Culture Street for tea at <strong>Shin Old Tea House</strong>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">6:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Korean BBQ Dinner:</strong> Taste charcoal-grilled Jeju pork at <strong>Geumdwaeji Sikdang (Gold Pig)</strong>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">8:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>N Seoul Tower:</strong> Cable car up Namsan Mountain to view the night skyline.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Day 3 -->
<div class="day-card">
    <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 3</span>
        <span class="day-title">Seongsu-dong, Han River Sunset &amp; Hanwoo Beef</span>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">10:30 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Seongsu-dong Exploration:</strong> Discover converted industrial warehouse cafes and fashion pop-ups in Seongsu-dong. Stop at <strong>Center Coffee</strong> or view <strong>Dior Seongsu</strong>.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">1:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Lunch at Maple Tree House:</strong> Premium table-side Korean BBQ featuring marbled Hanwoo beef in Itaewon.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">3:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Starfield Library &amp; COEX:</strong> Cross the river into Gangnam to view the massive 13-meter-tall wooden book towers.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">5:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Yeouido Hangang Park Sunset:</strong> Stroll the river banks, rent bicycles, and cook instant ramyeon at automated riverbank stations.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">8:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Dinner at Born &amp; Bred (2F Casual):</strong> Savor legendary native Korean Hanwoo beef in Majang-dong.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Day 4 -->
<div class="day-card">
    <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 4</span>
        <span class="day-title">Hongdae, Luxury Hot Spring Spa &amp; Hanok Cocktails</span>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">10:00 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Hongdae District:</strong> Walk through Hongdae's indie shopping streets, vintage fashion stores, and live busking spots.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">12:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Lunch at Kyochon Chicken 1991:</strong> Enjoy crisp Korean Fried Chicken (<em>Chimaek</em>) paired with soy garlic wings and cold draft beer.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">2:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Aquafield Goyang (Hot Spring Spa &amp; Thermal Pools):</strong> Spend 3.5 to 4 unhurried hours at one of Seoul's top thermal spas. Enjoy outdoor foot-soaks, mineral pools, cypress rooms, and relaxation lounges.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">7:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Upscale Modern Korean Dinner:</strong> Dine at <strong>Hansikgonggan</strong> or <strong>Sowoon</strong> for elevated Korean cuisine.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">9:30 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Nightcaps in Ikseon-dong:</strong> Sip craft cocktails or traditional <em>makgeolli</em> inside a converted 1920s hanok bar like <strong>Bar Cham</strong> or <strong>Eeo-duk</strong>.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Day 5 -->
<div class="day-card">
    <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 5</span>
        <span class="day-title">Relaxed Morning, Souvenirs &amp; Departure</span>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">10:00 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Hotel Check-Out:</strong> Sleep in and pack bags stress-free at Nine Tree Premier Myeongdong.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">10:30 AM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Lotte Department Store Food Hall:</strong> Walk through the basement food hall to pick up high-end tea sets, cosmetics, or packaged Korean snacks.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">12:00 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Farewell Lunch at Han-ilkwan:</strong> Enjoy classic Seoul-style marinated <em>Bulgogi</em> cooked on a brass dome grill.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">1:45 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>AREX Express to Airport:</strong> Board the non-stop express train straight to Incheon Terminal 1.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="time">5:15 PM</div>
            <div class="details"><strong>Flight Home:</strong> Depart on <strong>American Airlines AA 280</strong> back to Dallas (DFW).</div>
        </div>
    </div>
